1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,369
What does a p-value actually tell you?

2
00:00:02,819 --> 00:00:08,771
It's the probability of getting a result at least as extreme as yours, if the null hypothesis is true.

3
00:00:09,021 --> 00:00:10,685
Not the chance the null is true.

4
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:12,501
Then the rule is simple.

5
00:00:12,751 --> 00:00:15,865
If p ≤ alpha, reject H0.

6
00:00:16,115 --> 00:00:18,718
If p > alpha, fail to reject it.

7
00:00:19,168 --> 00:00:24,501
Both cards were made from notes, and each one points to the line it came from, so you can check it.

8
00:00:24,751 --> 00:00:26,159
Try it on your own notes.

